      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">124</data>
      <data key="d13">136</data>
      <data key="d14">def write_jsonl(path: Path, rows: Iterable[Any]) -&gt; int:</data>
      <data key="d15">Stream `rows` to `path` as JSONL; return how many were written.

    newline="\n" (ISS-28) + atomic: a crash mid-write must not leave a truncated
    last line that read_jsonl's json.loads then dies on. Streaming means `rows`
    may be a generator (build_chunks) that is never fully materialised.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
