      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1514</data>
      <data key="d13">1528</data>
      <data key="d14">def _read_capped(stream, limit: int) -&gt; tuple[bytes, bool]:</data>
      <data key="d15">Read at most `limit` bytes from `stream`, and report whether there were more.

    Reads one byte past the cap deliberately: that byte is the only way to tell
    "the output was exactly `limit` bytes" from "the output was larger and we
    stopped early" without reading the rest of it -- and not reading the rest of
    it is the entire point (ISS-236).</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
