      <data key="d14">def _origin_header_allowed(value: str | None, allowed_hostnames: frozenset[str]) -&gt; bool:</data>
      <data key="d15">Whether an `Origin` header, if present, names an accepted hostname.

    No `Origin` header at all is allowed -- that is the common case for
    non-browser clients (curl, an MCP client library) and carries none of the
    cross-origin-browser risk this check exists for. A present-but-unparseable
    or cross-origin value is refused.</data>
