      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">845</data>
      <data key="d13">861</data>
      <data key="d14">def _fit_lines(text: str, limit: int, measure: Callable[[str], int] = len) -&gt; str:</data>
      <data key="d15">The longest whole-line prefix of `text` that fits in `limit` units.

    The candidate is measured whole rather than line by line, so a measure that
    is not additive (any token estimate) is applied to the string that will
    actually be emitted. With the default `len` this is exactly the running
    "len(line) + a newline" arithmetic it replaces.</data>
