    <node id="sym:scripts/version_surfaces.py::release_commit_paths">
      <data key="d0">sym:scripts/version_surfaces.py::release_commit_paths</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">release_commit_paths</data>
      <data key="d10">release_commit_paths</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">scripts/version_surfaces.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">197</data>
      <data key="d13">210</data>
      <data key="d14">def release_commit_paths() -&gt; tuple[str, ...]:</data>
      <data key="d15">What `publish.yml` must include in the release commit.

    `bumped_paths()` plus `CHANGELOG.md`, which `bump_version.bump_changelog`
    rewrites but which is deliberately *not* a checked surface: before a bump its
    only version header is `[Unreleased]`, so a check demanding the current
    version would be red on every ordinary commit.

    publish.yml reads this rather than restating the list, because a hand-typed
    `--files` that misses a path produces the worst outcome available here -- a
    release commit that bumps some surfaces and not others, on a tag that cannot
    be reused.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="2067.75" y="1576.60" width="139.15" height="29.90" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
