      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_answer_limits.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">157</data>
      <data key="d13">177</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss241_many_small_deltas_are_capped_in_total(monkeypatch, capsys):</data>
      <data key="d15">Axis 2: a well-framed stream of small deltas stops at the ceiling.

    Every line here is short and valid, so the per-line bound never binds; only
    the running total can stop this stream. 9000 deltas of 1000 characters is
    ~9.2 MB on the wire against an 8 MiB ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
