      <data key="d12">96</data>
      <data key="d13">114</data>
      <data key="d14">def _invalid_byte_source() -&gt; bytes:</data>
      <data key="d15">Three exactly-_LIMIT-byte slices, the middle one not UTF-8 at all.

    0xFF can never begin a UTF-8 sequence, so it is not a truncated character to
    carry forward -- it must still be skipped, must be counted, and must not
    stall the loop or cost the slices around it.</data>
