      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">168</data>
      <data key="d13">188</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss236_the_byte_cap_stops_the_read_and_the_child_is_reaped(tmp_path, monkeypatch):</data>
      <data key="d15">The cap has to bind *during* the read. A child with far more to say than
    the cap allows must be cut off mid-write, killed and waited for -- not read
    to EOF and trimmed afterwards, which is what capture_output=True did.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
