      <data key="d14">def test_crlf_injection_in_cors_headers_is_sanitized(make_server):</data>
      <data key="d15">CodeQL alerts #8/#9: CRLF in Origin and Access-Control-Request-Headers
    must be stripped so an attacker cannot inject arbitrary response headers.

    Python's http.client rejects CRLF in headers on the *client* side, so we
    must use a raw socket to actually deliver the malicious header to the server.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">11</data>
