      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1010</data>
      <data key="d13">1033</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss243_a_crlf_in_the_oidc_issuer_cannot_inject_a_response_header(make_server):</data>
      <data key="d15">Issue 243: `_challenge()` interpolates oidc_issuer into WWW-Authenticate.

    Operator-supplied, so not remotely exploitable -- but the module states a
    rule for header values and this path did not follow it. The fix is
    structural: `_send_json` sanitises every extra header, so the rule holds
    for call sites nobody has written yet.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">16</data>
