      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1036</data>
      <data key="d13">1057</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss249_a_chunked_request_body_is_refused_with_411(make_server):</data>
      <data key="d15">Issue 249: Content-Length is the only framing `_read_body` understands.

    A chunked body measured as zero bytes was never read, so a spec-legal
    client got "expected a JSON-RPC object" and a socket still holding its
    request. Refusing the encoding by name says what is actually wrong.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">14</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
