    <node id="sym:tests/test_http_transport.py::test_a_missing_index_does_not_tell_the_caller_where_it_looked">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_http_transport.py::test_a_missing_index_does_not_tell_the_caller_where_it_looked</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_a_missing_index_does_not_tell_the_caller_where_it_looked</data>
      <data key="d10">test_a_missing_index_does_not_tell_the_caller_where_it_looked</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_http_transport.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">1108</data>
      <data key="d13">1148</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_a_missing_index_does_not_tell_the_caller_where_it_looked(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">503 must not carry the host's filesystem layout.

    `open_index` raises SystemExit with a message written for an operator at a
    terminal, naming the absolute index directory twice. Relaying str(exc) put
    that in a JSON-RPC error -- and therefore into the context window of any
    agent driving this server -- which is the disclosure `_public_repo_label`
    already refuses one endpoint over. The operator's detail belongs in the
    audit log, which is server-side.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d17">45</data>
