      <data key="d12">1620</data>
      <data key="d13">1640</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss203_http_only_without_a_port_refuses_instead_of_serving_stdio(mini_repo, monkeypatch):</data>
      <data key="d15">The flag names what to omit, so alone it asks for no transport at all.

    The test used to live inside the block that builds the HTTP transport, so
    with no --http-port that block never ran, the flag was never read, and main
    fell through to the stdio `serve()` -- precisely the transport --http-only
    exists to suppress, and with no diagnostic.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
