    <node id="sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::_js_regex">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::_js_regex</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_js_regex</data>
      <data key="d10">_js_regex</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_prod_igy.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">380</data>
      <data key="d13">391</data>
      <data key="d14">def _js_regex(content: str, name: str, arg: str) -&gt; re.Pattern:</data>
      <data key="d15">Pull a `const &lt;name&gt; = /&lt;pattern&gt;/i.test(&lt;arg&gt;)` literal out of the script.

    The retarget guard is the one piece of prod-igy whose *behaviour* is worth
    asserting rather than its source text, and the pytest environment has no
    Node (see this module's docstring). Extracting the literal and compiling it
    with `re` tests the pattern itself: a typo in the login shape fails here
    instead of silently retargeting a release PR in production.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1277.97" y="3331.70" width="88.88" height="29.25" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_js_regex</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_prod_igy_never_retargets_a_release_pr">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_prod_igy.py::test_prod_igy_never_retargets_a_release_pr</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">test_prod_igy_never_retargets_a_release_pr</data>
      <data key="d10">test_prod_igy_never_retargets_a_release_pr</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_prod_igy.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">394</data>
      <data key="d13">418</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_prod_igy_never_retargets_a_release_pr():</data>
      <data key="d15">A release PR must stay on `main`.

    publish.yml has prod-igy raise `release/vX.Y.Z -&gt; main` and then polls for
    that merge, so retargeting it to `develop` strands the version bump and
    times the release run out with nothing merged.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1390.85" y="3331.70" width="136.12" height="29.25" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">test_prod_igy_…</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
