      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_repo2graph.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">773</data>
      <data key="d13">794</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_iss245_manifest_defaults_when_the_graph_never_went_through_build(tmp_path):</data>
      <data key="d15">write_manifest has only ever duck-typed `g`, and a Graph assembled by
    hand has no build to inherit a fan-out limit from. It must still write a
    manifest stating the default rather than raising: a wrong number is the
    #245 bug, but no manifest at all is worse than one carrying the default.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="2785.65" y="3788.35" width="151.25" height="32.50" />
