      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_secrets_hardening.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">222</data>
      <data key="d13">240</data>
      <data key="d14">def test_scan_content_secrets_returns_spans_not_plaintext():</data>
      <data key="d15">A finding locates a credential; it must never carry one.

    Callers only count findings or report `f[0]`, so returning the matched
    bytes built a list of live credentials that existed solely to be thrown
    away -- and any later `emit(..., findings=findings)` would have shipped it
    verbatim. Offsets below are hand-counted against `text`: "tok = '" is 7
    characters, and the token is 36.</data>
      <data key="d16">true</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="4266.10" y="4161.15" width="133.10" height="28.60" />
