    <node id="sym:tests/test_vectors.py::rigged_order">
      <data key="d0">sym:tests/test_vectors.py::rigged_order</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">rigged_order</data>
      <data key="d10">rigged_order</data>
      <data key="d11">function</data>
      <data key="d3">tests/test_vectors.py</data>
      <data key="d4">python</data>
      <data key="d12">65</data>
      <data key="d13">75</data>
      <data key="d14">def rigged_order(candidates):</data>
      <data key="d15">The dense ranking this suite rigs: BM25 rank 2 first, rank 1 third.

    Swapping only ranks 1 and 2 is not enough -- reciprocal rank fusion gives
    the two chunks identical fused scores and the outcome turns on a tie-break.
    Demoting the BM25 winner to dense rank 3 makes the intended chunk win
    outright, whatever the tie-break rule is.</data>
      <data key="d_nodegraphics">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="2307.43" y="4382.00" width="107.50" height="27.95" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">rigged_order</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
